 # Packet-Plumber-UE
-Initial commit placeholder — the bootstrap minion scaffolds the project.
+
+**Packet Plumber — Unreal Engine comparison build.** A second implementation
+of the Packet Plumber game on UE 5.8.x, built to compare against the Odin v2
+build (`/Users/moses/code/packet-plumber`) and decide by evidence which
+engine carries the full game.
+
+The game design is the existing PP GDD — **same game, second engine**. This
+repo does not re-decide design; it ports the spine: routing canon [RR]
+(per-hop forwarding, ECMP, bundles) and the determinism rules [ODN-*] carry
+over as requirements.
+
+## Mission and status
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Engine | UE **5.8.x** (official MCP plugin lives here; 5.9 is in development — see `docs/research-report.md` for the timeline + upgrade path) |
+| Language | **C++-first** (agents can't diff Blueprints). Blueprints only where unavoidable, documented. |
+| Determinism spine | Ported + verified: ODN-9 RNG (PCG32 + splitmix64), ODN-11 FNV-1a-64 + LE serialization, replay-equality. `tests/build/spine-check` reproduces the Odin pinned vectors byte-exact and asserts the committed golden engine-free (check count is counted at runtime — no engine needed). |
+| MCP | Community **UE-MCP** wired via `.mcp.json` (stdio); official **Unreal MCP** plugin enabled in the project. See `docs/agent-playbook.md`. |
+| CI | `scripts/local-ci.sh` — format / spine / static gates run without the engine; build / tests / probe / golden gates activate when UE 5.8 is installed (`scripts/install-engine.sh`). |
+| Engine installed? | **Yes — UE 5.8.1 installed** (2026-08-20); the full 7-gate suite runs green incl. build + 8/8 automation tests + PPProbe + 3-way golden compare |
+
+## Repo map
+
+```
+PacketPlumberUE.uproject   UE 5.8 project (modules + MCP plugins enabled)
+.mcp.json                  UE-MCP server wiring (repo-root project MCP config)
+Config/                    DefaultEngine.ini pins the fixed 20 Hz sim tick (ODN-2)
+Source/
+  PacketPlumberCore/       the pure sim spine (PP_Rng, PP_Hash, PP_SimState,
+                           PP_Sim) — UE-header-free by design, dual-runner;
+                           public headers in Public/PacketPlumberCore/
+  PacketPlumberCoreTests/  UE automation tests (the determinism suite)
+  PacketPlumberEditor/     PPProbe commandlet (headless spine probe)
+  PacketPlumber/           game module (slice-1 grows it)
+tests/spine_check.cpp      standalone runner over the SAME spine headers
+scripts/                   local-ci.sh, run-tests-headless.sh, install-engine.sh,
+                           format-check.sh, static-check.py, compare-golden.sh
+docs/                      research-report.md (comparison + slice-1 scope),
+                           agent-playbook.md (MCP/vision loop), goldens/
+AGENTS.md                  agent rules (AI-workflow optimization)
+```
+
+## Quickstart
+
+```bash
+scripts/install-engine.sh        # status; prints the one-time manual install
+scripts/local-ci.sh --fast       # pre-engine gates: format, spine, static
+scripts/local-ci.sh              # full suite (engine gates skip until UE 5.8 lands)
+```
+
+First engine build: **30-60+ min** (module compile + toolchain warmup);
+incremental builds 5-15 min. Timing expectations per gate are in
+`scripts/local-ci.sh` and recorded per run in `docs/timings.md`.
+
+Headless verification without the editor GUI:
+
+```bash
+tests/build/spine-check                      # the determinism conformance runner
+# engine-gated (after install):
+scripts/run-tests-headless.sh --tests        # Automation RunTests PacketPlumber
+scripts/run-tests-headless.sh --probe        # -run=PPProbe -seed=42 -ticks=100
+```
+
+## Binary strategy
+
+`*.uasset / *.umap / *.ubulk / *.uexp` are **git-lfs** tracked
+(`.gitattributes`); everything generated (`Binaries/ Intermediate/
+DerivedDataCache/ Saved/`) is git-ignored. Decide LFS adoption with the
+first real asset: `git lfs install` once, then commit as usual.
+
+## Comparison mission
+
+The Odin v2 build is the reference implementation (same GDD, same routing
+canon, byte-identical replay spine). This repo is the evidence track for
+engine choice: agent drivability, iteration speed, headless testability,
+build times, binary size, platform reach. The criteria, the UE 5.9 timeline,
+the MCP landscape and the recommended slice-1 scope are in
+`docs/research-report.md` — user-reviewed, the gate before any architecture
+work.
