+# Agent Playbook — driving the UE editor through MCP
+
+*2026-08-20 · bootstrap. The MCP wiring + the screenshot loop, as recipes
+an agent (this repo's minions, Gru/Silas, Perkins) can follow.*
+
+## The two servers, and when to use which
+
+| | **UE-MCP (community — wired)** | **Unreal MCP (official — enabled, needs editor)** |
+|---|---|---|
+| Config | `.mcp.json` at the repo root (stdio) | generated per client: `ModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig <Client>` → `.mcp.json` entry (`"type": "http", "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp"`) |
+| Needs the editor? | bridge actions need it; filesystem reads (INI, C++ headers, asset listing) work with it CLOSED | server runs INSIDE the editor — editor must be up |
+| Transport | stdio (`npx -y ue-mcp PacketPlumberUE.uproject`) | HTTP + SSE, loopback only (127.0.0.1:8000), no auth |
+| Surface | 24 categories / 783+ actions + Epic's 830-tool native registry (5.8) | engine toolset registry (Python/C++ toolsets) |
+| Guard rails | write guards, source-control guard, flow rollback, idempotency | none built-in — loopback-only by design |
+| Maturity | experimental community (MIT), fast-moving | Experimental (5.8), Epic-supported; the 5.9/6.0 path |
+
+**Decision (bootstrap D3):** agents in this repo use **UE-MCP** for
+editor-driving; the official server is enabled and ready — the 5.9 upgrade
+re-visits it (expanded plugin + Epic Developer Assistant).
+
+## Starting the editor for MCP
+
+```bash
+# from the repo root, with UE 5.8 installed:
+"/Users/Shared/Epic Games/UE_5.8/Engine/Binaries/Mac/UnrealEditor" \
+  "$(pwd)/PacketPlumberUE.uproject" \
+  -ModelContextProtocolStartServer &      # official server up on :8000
+```
+
+UE-MCP bridge: the C++ bridge plugin is deployed by `npx ue-mcp init`
+once (first run; requires a compile on editor launch). The server in
+`.mcp.json` retries the bridge (`ws://127.0.0.1:9877`) in the background —
+start the editor first, then call MCP tools.
+
+Diagnostics: `npx ue-mcp doctor` (most first-run failures = editor not
+restarted after init, bridge compile error in the Output Log
+`UE_MCP_Bridge`, or the editor on a different project).
+
+## Proven agent commands (this machine, 2026-08-20)
+
+```bash
+npx -y ue-mcp --help        # boots the server: 27 tools + 1615 flow tasks,
+                            # wraps the 830-tool Epic 5.8 registry snapshot
+```
+
+Editor-gated (record on the first editor run, then paste results here):
+
+- Asset query (works editor-closed): `project.get_status`,
+  `asset.list`/`asset.query` categories.
+- Screenshot loop (the harness T2 equivalent):
+  1. `editor.capture_screenshot` (target `viewport` / `pie` / `window`)
+  2. PNG lands on disk → verify with `bin/vision-read <image> "<prompt>"`
+     (the repo's vision entry point: fails loudly unless
+     `VISION_READ_BACKEND` is set, or open the PNG with the pi `read` tool
+     — never guess image content; flash/glm have no native vision)
+  3. Compare against the golden set (docs/goldens/ when pixel goldens
+     arrive with slice-1)
+- Build: `project.build` (configuration Development) — flows
+  (`flow(action="run", flowName=...)`) for multi-step sequences.
+
+## Security rules
+
+- Both servers are **loopback-only / unauthenticated** — never expose the
+  port, never run them on a shared machine, never forward.
+- The loopback trust model assumes only local processes can reach
+  127.0.0.1. A **same-host browser** (any page you visit) can also issue
+  requests to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp` (origin confusion / DNS
+  rebinding-style reads) — never keep the editor's MCP server running while
+  browsing untrusted sites.
+- The bridge has write guards — keep them ON; treat the source-control
+  guard as mandatory for checked-in assets.
+- Agent writes to the project are code review surface: MCP-driven changes
+  ship in a PR, never silently in `Saved/`.
