+# Project Context — Packet-Plumber-UE
+
+*2026-08-20 · bootstrap (packet-plumber-ue-bootstrap). Companion to
+`AGENTS.md` (the agent contract) — this doc is the wider picture: why the
+repo exists, what the comparison track must prove, and the current state.*
+
+## Why this repo exists
+
+The user wants a second Packet Plumber implementation on Unreal Engine to
+compare against the Odin v2 build (`/Users/moses/code/packet-plumber`) and
+**decide by evidence** which engine carries the full game. Requirements
+(2026-08-20): UE 5.9-targeted, MCP set up, optimized for AI-agent workflow.
+Reality: 5.9 is confirmed-in-development (Unreal Fest Seoul 2026) but not
+released (~Nov/Dec 2026). **Therefore: scaffold on UE 5.8.x now (official
+MCP plugin v1 lives there), pin the 5.9 upgrade path.**
+
+## The comparison track (what must be evidenced)
+
+The Odin v2 build is the reference: deterministic spine (ODN-1..18), byte-
+identical replay, golden-image harness, ~1s local gates. The UE build must
+be comparable on:
+
+1. **Agent drivability** — MCP surface (official Unreal MCP vs community
+   UE-MCP), C++-first diffability, editor-driving commands.
+2. **Iteration speed** — build times (UE: 30-60+ min first build vs Odin's
+   seconds), Live Coding, hot reload, asset workflow.
+3. **Headless testability** — Unreal Automation Tests + commandlets
+   (`-run=PPProbe`) vs Odin's harness.
+4. **Build times** — measured per gate in `docs/timings.md`.
+5. **Binary size** — packaged game footprint (UE ~100MB+ vs raylib ~MBs).
+6. **Platform reach** — UE: PC/Mac/Linux/iOS/Android/consoles/Switch 2;
+   Odin+raylib: desktop + DIY web/mobile.
+
+The criteria, findings, and the recommended slice-1 scope are the subject
+of `docs/research-report.md` — **user-reviewed via lavish; the gate before
+any architecture work.**
+
+## Determinism spine (ported + verified)
+
+| ODN rule | UE port | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| ODN-9 owned PRNG | `PP::FRng` (PCG32 XSH-RR + splitmix64) | ✅ green — pinned vectors reproduce the Odin reference byte-exact (seed 0/42) |
+| ODN-11 FNV-1a-64 + LE serialization | `PP::Fnv1a64`, `PP::SerializeState` | ✅ green — versioned header "PPUE", field-by-field LE |
+| ODN-11 replay equality | `PP::Step` + `PP::StateHash` | ✅ green — same seed+ticks → identical hash; different seed diverges |
+| ODN-2 fixed 20 Hz tick | `Config/DefaultEngine.ini` | ✅ pinned (engine-gated verification pending install) |
+| ODN-1 sim/presentation separation | spine headers are UE-header-free (dual-runner) | ✅ by construction |
+
+The dual-runner design is the keystone: the SAME headers compile in the
+engine module and in `tests/build/spine-check` (plain g++), so the
+determinism contract is provable **before the engine exists on the
+machine** — and any future port (server validator, wasm, other engine) has
+a conformance test waiting.
+
+## MCP wiring (current state)
+
+- **Wired (committed):** community **UE-MCP** (db-lyon/ue-mcp) in
+  `.mcp.json` — stdio (`npx -y ue-mcp PacketPlumberUE.uproject`), 24
+  categories / 783+ actions, wraps Epic's 830-tool native registry on 5.8,
+  filesystem reads work editor-closed, write-guards + flow rollback.
+  Verified: server boots and registers tools on this machine.
+- **Enabled in-project (engine-gated):** official **Unreal MCP** plugin
+  (`ModelContextProtocol`) + `PythonScriptPlugin` in
+  `PacketPlumberUE.uproject`; server start via
+  `-ModelContextProtocolStartServer` or console
+  `ModelContextProtocol.StartServer`; client config via
+  `ModelContextProtocol.GenerateClientConfig <Client>`.
+- **Why community-first:** stdio transport (works with pi's MCP adapter
+  today), editor-closed reads, guard rails. Official is the 5.9/6.0 native
+  path — its HTTP/SSE loopback server needs a running editor.
+- **Screenshot loop:** `editor.capture_screenshot` (UE-MCP) → PNG →
+  `bin/vision-read` (the repo's vision entry point; fails loudly unless a
+  backend is configured — never guess image content) — the harness
+  T2-pixel-golden equivalent. Recipe in `docs/agent-playbook.md`.
+
+## Current state (2026-08-20)
+
+**Report gate: PASSED (lavish review, 2026-08-20).** User rulings:
+- R1: Accept UE-MCP (community) as the wired server — official enabled-but-dormant ✓
+- R2: Approve the 3-slice comparison scope ✓
+- R3: Install UE 5.8 now — run the full loop ✓ (launcher prep via brew; login + engine download are the user's manual step)
+- R4: git-lfs for uassets ✓ (`git lfs install` done)
+- Review addendum: the user's motivation is "would UE look better" — the report now carries a **visual ceiling** axis + a side-by-side visual probe (same scene, both engines) in slice-2.
+
+- [x] Repo + GitHub (`solarity-services/Packet-Plumber-UE`), UE 5.8 C++
+  project scaffold (4 modules + 2 targets + commandlet), LFS strategy.
+- [x] Determinism spine port — standalone runner green, engine-free
+  (pinned vectors + committed-golden assertions; check count runtime-counted).
+- [x] Local CI suite — pre-engine gates green; **full 7-gate suite green on
+  UE 5.8.1** (2026-08-20): build + 8/8 automation tests + PPProbe + 3-way
+  golden compare (engine probe == standalone == committed golden).
+- [x] MCP wiring (community server verified booting) + official plugin
+  enabled in-project.
+- [x] Research report drafted → lavish review (the gate).
+- [x] Engine install (UE 5.8.1) → first full-suite run with timings
+  (`docs/timings.md`).
+- [ ] 5.9 upgrade when it ships.
+
+## Links
