+  <section class="mb-10">
+    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">4 · Determinism in UE vs the ODN spine</h2>
+
+    <div class="alert alert-success mb-4">
+      <span><b>The port already works.</b> <code>tests/build/spine-check</code> compiles the SAME headers the engine module uses (deliberately UE-header-free) and asserts the Odin pinned vectors byte-exact — the cross-language conformance test (ODN-9, arch REVIEW m6) passing before the engine is even installed. seed 0 → <code>2196338726 … 209995402</code>; seed 42 → <code>2399007886 …</code> — identical to Odin.</span>
+    </div>
+
+    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-content/5 bg-base-100 mb-4">
+      <table class="table table-zebra table-md">
+        <thead><tr><th>ODN spine requirement</th><th>UE reality</th><th>Port decision</th></tr></thead>
+        <tbody>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-9</b> owned PRNG, pinned vectors</td><td>FRandomStream exists (SRand-based, seedable) but is engine-internal and drifts across versions</td><td><b class="text-success">Port PP::FRng</b> (PCG32 XSH-RR + splitmix64) — proven byte-identical; engine RNG never enters sim state paths</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-10</b> integer math</td><td>C++ integers are bit-identical across targets; floats mostly IEEE but SIMD/vectorized paths can vary; ParallelFor is unordered</td><td>Integer-only state paths; no ParallelFor/async in sim; floats stay in the view — the same rule as Odin</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-10</b> array-only iteration</td><td>TMap/TSet iteration order is hash-based/unspecified; TArray is insertion-ordered</td><td>Arrays + insertion order in sim state paths; maps for lookups only</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-2</b> fixed 20 Hz tick</td><td><code>bUseFixedFrameRate</code> + <code>FixedFrameRate</code> engine settings; explicit stepping fully portable</td><td>Both: config pins 20 Hz for PIE; <code>PP::Step(Tick)</code> advances the sim explicitly — never depends on frame timing</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-11</b> LE binary save, versioned header</td><td>FArchive/FMemoryWriter is on-platform deterministic but engine-versioned layout</td><td><b class="text-success">Explicit field-by-field LE writer</b> (ported) — keeps the cross-runner golden contract, 5.9-proof</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-11</b> replay equality</td><td>Engine Replay System (UDemoNetDriver) targets networked demos — netcode-coupled</td><td>Action-log re-step — simpler, byte-exact, runs in automation tests</td></tr>
+          <tr><td><b>ODN-17</b> golden images</td><td>Viewport rendering is GPU-dependent — not bit-stable across GPUs/drivers</td><td>MCP screenshot + vision-read (semantic) for editor visuals; the SIM stays hash-verified (it never renders)</td></tr>
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+    </div>
